{
  "id": "can_place_flowers",
  "title": "Can Place Flowers",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Algorithms",
  "tags": [
    "Array",
    "Greedy"
  ],
  "description": "<p>You have a long flowerbed in which some of the plots are planted, and some are not. However, flowers cannot be planted in <strong>adjacent</strong> plots.</p> <p>Given an integer array <code>flowerbed</code> containing <code>0</code>'s and <code>1</code>'s, where <code>0</code> means empty and <code>1</code> means not empty, and an integer <code>n</code>, return <code>true</code> <em>if</em> <code>n</code> <em>new flowers can be planted in the</em> <code>flowerbed</code> <em>without violating the no-adjacent-flowers rule and</em> <code>false</code> <em>otherwise</em>.</p> <p> </p> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> flowerbed = [1,0,0,0,1], n = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> true\n</pre><p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> flowerbed = [1,0,0,0,1], n = 2\n<strong>Output:</strong> false\n</pre> <p> </p> <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>1 &lt;= flowerbed.length &lt;= 2 * 10<sup>4</sup></code></li> <li><code>flowerbed[i]</code> is <code>0</code> or <code>1</code>.</li> <li>There are no two adjacent flowers in <code>flowerbed</code>.</li> <li><code>0 &lt;= n &lt;= flowerbed.length</code></li> </ul>",
  "hints": [],
  "method": {
    "name": "canPlaceFlowers",
    "returnType": "auto",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "flowerbed",
        "type": "array"
      },
      {
        "name": "n",
        "type": "int"
      }
    ]
  },
